  "term": "substitution test",
  "definition": "In this packet, a substitution test refers to the Digit Symbol Substitution Test (DSST), a scale used as part of cognitive assessment in older adults. It was used to measure cognitive performance, with lower DSST scores treated as reflecting worse cognitive function, particularly executive functioning.",
